From: AX50 OpenWrt bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] wave: keep the exclusive monitor out of software iftypes

The monitor consumes the native firmware master and requires exclusive
ownership of both physical radios.  It is not an unrestricted software
interface, so advertise it only in interface_modes.

OpenWrt uses software monitor support to distinguish mac80211 from full-MAC
devices.  Setting that bit made it skip reuse of WAVE's persistent AP master
and attempt to create a second AP with the same name, breaking ordinary AP
startup on the monitor-capable radio.

The supported single monitor remains admitted by cfg80211 interface_modes;
single interface types do not belong in iface_combinations.  The existing
whole-card claim still rejects AP, station, scan and CAC coexistence.  Keep
the AP combinations and genuinely software AP-VLAN type unchanged.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/cfg80211.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/cfg80211.c
@@ -2891,8 +2891,10 @@
   wiphy->interface_modes = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP);
   if (radio_id == 0 && wave_hw_monitor_supported(HANDLE_T_PTR(mtlk_hw_t, hw_handle))) {
     wiphy->interface_modes |= BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR);
-    wiphy->software_iftypes |= BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR);
+    /* This receiver owns the firmware master and both radios exclusively.
+     * It is a hardware mode, not an unrestricted software interface. Keep
+     * full-MAC master reuse and the existing AP combinations intact. */
   }
 #if !MTLK_USE_DIRECTCONNECT_DP_API && !MTLK_USE_PUMA6_UDMA
   wiphy->interface_modes |= BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN);
   wiphy->software_iftypes |= BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN);
